1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:04,011
Axion Kitchen: quantum optimization for catering production.

2
00:00:04,152 --> 00:00:08,374
We completed the factory baselines in four and eight hours, both
checked optimal.

3
00:00:08,515 --> 00:00:14,445
Our extension chooses shared batch yields, allocations, equipment,
qualified workers and phase times.

4
00:00:14,586 --> 00:00:18,229
Cookers are machines, cleaning is setup, and departures are due dates.

5
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:22,303
Freshness, calendars, outages and committed work constrain replanning.

6
00:00:22,444 --> 00:00:25,802
Complete meals come first, then waste, batches and changes.

7
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,311
Two customers each need ten meals.

8
00:00:28,461 --> 00:00:30,103
Main A is already cooking.

9
00:00:30,253 --> 00:00:32,941
A shared twenty-portion side batch can serve both.

10
00:00:33,091 --> 00:00:37,315
But the side and one Main B option want cooker C2 at the same time.

11
00:00:37,465 --> 00:00:43,140
The checked QAOA plan pairs that side with a different Main B program
on C1.

12
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:45,039
Both orders depart complete.

13
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:51,820
Remove only the side batch.

14
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:56,130
Neither order receives a complete meal; twenty main portions are
wasted.

15
00:00:56,280 --> 00:01:00,781
This checked manual intervention shows why the objective couples main
and side.

16
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:07,733
A bit selects a locally valid batch: its quantity, allocations,
resources and times.

17
00:01:07,882 --> 00:01:12,788
Programs with the same anchor share demand, so a block chooses one
program or idle.

18
00:01:12,937 --> 00:01:15,074
Cross-block penalties exclude clashes.

19
00:01:15,223 --> 00:01:20,878
In the code, product expands coverage products; coefficient span plus
one sets the penalty.

20
00:01:21,027 --> 00:01:24,450
This cell uses thirty-two programs and three idle bits.

21
00:01:24,599 --> 00:01:27,734
Restricted portfolios can exclude better schedules.

22
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:34,919
Main coverage times side coverage gives complete service; their sum
minus twice the product counts unpaired food.

23
00:01:35,069 --> 00:01:39,399
Both coverages are linear in batch bits, so the objective stays
quadratic.

24
00:01:39,549 --> 00:01:42,856
Each priority weight dominates all lower costs combined.

25
00:01:43,006 --> 00:01:47,806
For hard constraints, P equals the full objective coefficient span
plus one.

26
00:01:47,956 --> 00:01:51,391
A violation therefore cannot beat any feasible schedule.

27
00:01:51,541 --> 00:01:55,466
This guarantees feasible ground states, not heuristic convergence.

28
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,130
A repaired cooker still needs cleaning.

29
00:01:58,277 --> 00:02:05,298
Here the qualified worker first finishes committed work, then cleans
the repaired cooker from eleven forty to eleven fifty.

30
00:02:05,445 --> 00:02:07,476
Both worker and cooker are reserved.

31
00:02:07,623 --> 00:02:13,761
The independent checker reconstructs these intervals, freshness and
meal handovers from raw schedule records.

32
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:20,151
Return to the original batch choices and run the trained depth-three
QAOA circuit locally.

33
00:02:20,301 --> 00:02:24,354
Cost and conflict phases alternate with blockwise XY mixing.

34
00:02:24,504 --> 00:02:29,709
The mixer preserves one choice per block; the independent checker
rejects physical clashes.

35
00:02:29,859 --> 00:02:33,614
We draw four thousand ninety-six fresh samples with saved angles.

36
00:02:33,764 --> 00:02:38,436
The receipt reports the best checked outcome, separately from the
retained kitchen replay.

37
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:44,196
We selected the QAOA configuration on the cell and S0/S1.

38
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:50,322
On held-out S2/S3, it finds the offered-pool optimum in all ten seeds
at both budgets.

39
00:02:50,465 --> 00:02:53,390
Random-angle search also hits all ten on S2.

40
00:02:53,534 --> 00:03:01,767
At two hundred fifty-six evaluations, median optimum probability per
shot is about eleven and twenty-two times random-angle search.

41
00:03:01,911 --> 00:03:03,776
Angles are optimized per instance.

42
00:03:03,919 --> 00:03:07,801
These restricted portfolios still exclude better full-grid schedules.

43
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:13,871
VQE uses Givens gates within blocks and controlled rotations between
coupled blocks.

44
00:03:14,019 --> 00:03:21,537
With exact CVaR and adjoint gradients, median optimum probability is
about twelve percent in both held-out cases.

45
00:03:21,685 --> 00:03:24,401
Budgets and shots differ from QAOA.

46
00:03:24,549 --> 00:03:27,748
The primary setup hits ten of ten and nine of ten seeds.

47
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:30,780
VeloxQ now drives the replanning loop.

48
00:03:30,930 --> 00:03:37,735
Start with its own full plan, free two blocks, solve the conditional
QUBO, and accept only a checked improvement.

49
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:43,837
Across three widths, missed meal lots fall from nine to seven, eleven
to six, and thirteen to seven.

50
00:03:43,987 --> 00:03:46,334
These runs used seventy-one submissions.

51
00:03:46,484 --> 00:03:52,436
Exact neighborhood controls match or improve final quality, and longer
classical runs remain better.

52
00:03:52,586 --> 00:03:55,210
This demonstrates integration, not a speedup.

53
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:57,858
The cell is deliberately small.

54
00:03:58,001 --> 00:04:01,362
Larger inputs generate eighteen thousand batch programs.

55
00:04:01,505 --> 00:04:04,743
Equipment, workers and paired demand couple their choices.

56
00:04:04,886 --> 00:04:07,789
We measure restriction loss and search quality separately.

57
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,543
What should the kitchen buy?

58
00:04:09,693 --> 00:04:14,023
In the larger case, a third cooker leaves best-found service at ninety
meals.

59
00:04:14,173 --> 00:04:19,997
A prep or packing helper raises it to one hundred ten: the existing
worker handles both jobs.

60
00:04:20,147 --> 00:04:25,054
We changed one resource at a time, using equal classical budgets and
two seeds.

61
00:04:25,204 --> 00:04:27,892
These are checked plans, not certified optima.

62
00:04:28,042 --> 00:04:30,837
Prices are still needed for an investment decision.

63
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:43,433
Our log records three decisions: correct repair cleaning, optimize
complete-meal service, and prove idle elimination.

64
00:04:43,583 --> 00:04:45,998
The checked cell serves twenty meals without waste.

65
00:04:46,147 --> 00:04:47,729
Benchmarks and code are linked.
